                    {
                        "sense_id": "faf3dd77-67f7-3f20-aa67-54177f754247",
                        "entry_id": "ba08fe10-7b3a-3e91-967e-b5ccdf09506a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A nickname for Saskatoon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea5d5657-3c4a-4a5b-9979-eaace64badf0",
                                "sense_id": "faf3dd77-67f7-3f20-aa67-54177f754247",
                                "text": "A stop in Saskatoon is celebrated with possibly the worst sandwich ever. […] I sleep whenever I can, and now that we have picked up new passengers in Toontown, I no longer have the row to myself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9d7f0c2-c0a6-4488-b898-3cafb1778215",
                                "sense_id": "faf3dd77-67f7-3f20-aa67-54177f754247",
                                "text": "Saskatoon could be a violent city. […] “Just do. You're well known around here—kinda famous, at least here in Toontown. Grumpy Comic Shop Guy.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46e004bf-40f1-4c3b-b797-9fd2c7919715",
                                "sense_id": "faf3dd77-67f7-3f20-aa67-54177f754247",
                                "text": "Toontown’s Shooting Guns (recent Juno nominees and champions of Hawkeyes), are also doing a 12-inch split vinyl release with the band."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "b8889e93-1608-3834-b8bb-89161d2281c1",
                "word": "ToonTown",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "032e227b-1f5e-3dbc-a995-fb0290b42534",
                        "entry_id": "b8889e93-1608-3834-b8bb-89161d2281c1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of Toontown."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c03b8e85-3615-4994-8e7e-ec9b6f203261",
                                "sense_id": "032e227b-1f5e-3dbc-a995-fb0290b42534",
                                "text": "Subdomain: ToonTown.sk.ca"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ec6ab78-3c39-4492-8e02-a6f59e86e5d1",
                                "sense_id": "032e227b-1f5e-3dbc-a995-fb0290b42534",
                                "text": "Radar Kids (Saskatoon, Radar Vision) This hard hitting trance duo hails from the Heartland of prairie raving, ToonTown."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ee60a4b-b45d-4b23-b40b-0b8b40e833a8",
                                "sense_id": "032e227b-1f5e-3dbc-a995-fb0290b42534",
                                "text": "Saskatoon, Winnipeg, Calgary and Edmonton (and others I'm sure) have both LNS's and Crafts Canada. […] Here in ToonTown two hobby/craft stores have gone out of business in the past 5 or so years."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49ab6b0c-8356-4bb9-8da3-8415bcfeeeae",
                                "sense_id": "032e227b-1f5e-3dbc-a995-fb0290b42534",
                                "text": "> Residents of Saskatoon, Saskatchewan, Canada. […]\nOne of the nicknames for our town is ToonTown, like the Big Apple or City of Angels, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae932453-9b67-4314-8891-b302d6f7719d",
                                "sense_id": "032e227b-1f5e-3dbc-a995-fb0290b42534",
                                "text": "By the vet college, I assume you mean the one at USask here in ToonTown? We live about 3 minutes away from there, and should you come up to Saskatoon will show you all and any hospitality."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6779df3-82ef-4240-a261-705c1ee3e651",
                                "sense_id": "032e227b-1f5e-3dbc-a995-fb0290b42534",
                                "text": "Come to think of it - you'll be near Lake Diefenbaker when you travel between Regina and Saskatoon. […] The Mendel is in ToonTown."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b108f37d-bbd0-46e4-bdaf-de68211500b8",
                                "sense_id": "032e227b-1f5e-3dbc-a995-fb0290b42534",
                                "text": ">>I'd like to inform anybody that does not know, the closing gas prices for\n>>most stations in Saskatoon tonight, was 91.9 cents/L. Martensville, […]\nIf you have a gas-hog that needs 14L/100 km on the highway, then driving 30 km each way from ToonTown to \"racetrac gas\" would consume about 8.4 L of gas - or about $7 worth of gas, depending on the exact price."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
